From 6dfa9e4c2286452454fca656bbb5b2775e1f0e5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:20:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gen4m: build and run the MT6897 Wi-Fi driver on Linux 7.x

- Kbuild: CONN_SRC for the conninfra/connfem headers, the compat header
  and no -Werror.
- cfg80211: adapters from the 7.x cfg80211_ops prototypes to the
  existing handlers (wireless_dev based key and station operations,
  link_id/radio_idx arguments, cfg80211_ap_update). Remain-on-channel
  and mgmt-tx keep the cookie that cfg80211 now allocates. Header
  prototypes follow the same version checks as their definitions.
- netdev: GRO lists moved under napi->gro, alloc_netdev_dummy(), void
  platform remove, the new ch_switch, new_sta and del_sta signatures,
  removed cfg80211_ap_settings fields, string MODULE_IMPORT_NS(),
  strscpy().
- Wireless-extension events become no-ops when the kernel has no WEXT;
  nl80211 carries them.

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
